  "body": "Found while working #1610 (PR #1699). An incomplete model (a STEP closed shell that meshes open) carries the fidelity-unknown sentinel and its hole (`schema::MeshOpen`) on the model only. A stock copied from it (`SetStock` FromModel, setup clones) carries the sentinel, so it is still refused at the post, but its refusal reads the hole from the source model by name (`mesh_open::unknown_note`). Once the source is deleted, the copy's refusal falls back to \"saved before CamCraft recorded mesh fidelity (project v58 or older)\", which is wrong words for that mesh.\n\nSafe today (still refused); only the message is misleading.\n\nDone means: a stock copy of an incomplete model keeps naming the hole after its source is deleted, across undo and save/load; pinned.\n",
